{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"dd854b0bdeb350d526d2b4d3c964b9e345931204021b7c3c896c29d7b18f460e","digest":{"component_or_area":"LLM provider seam and two-tier support policy","key_entities":["docs/adr/0059-llm-provider-seam-and-support-tiers.md","docs/llm-framework.md","docs/env-vars.md","provider_factory","ModelProfile","provider_provenance","KNOWN_PROVIDER_NAMES","capabilities.py","providers.py","bedrock_model.py","runner.py","REBAR_LLM_MODEL","REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION","ProviderSession","_GATEWAY_PROVIDER_NAMES","BedrockModelProfile","AnthropicModelProfile"],"problem_keywords":["ADR","documentation","provider seam","two-tier support policy","pydantic-ai","Bedrock","provider registry","capability decision","verdict provenance","first-class","best-effort"],"propositions":["The provider seam and two-tier support policy have been implemented across stories S1-S8 but lack an ADR recording decisions and rejected alternatives, causing the same arguments to resurface on future Bedrock/gateway requests.","docs/llm-framework.md contradicts the current implementation on provider resolution, tier handling, Bedrock support, and numeric defaults; it describes S4-era behavior as future and omits the provider registry entirely.","An ADR must record rejected alternatives with evidence: in-process LiteLLM, gateway-fronted Bedrock, refusing off-tier verdicts, SSM long-term keys, and cross-provider fallback; without this record, LiteLLM and gateway options will be re-proposed.","The tier model (first_class vs best_effort) is derived from configuration-time facts (base_url, via_gateway) and stamped into unsigned sidecar provenance; the ADR must record what a consumer can infer and what cryptographic guarantees do not exist.","Operational findings from Bedrock verification—IMDS hop-limit reachability, region resolution via AWS_DEFAULT_REGION, caching profiles, and silent model-dependent failures—must be recorded so they are not rediscovered in future work.","docs/env-vars.md, README.md, and docs/llm-framework.md require corrections to remove contradictions, stale line anchors, missing Bedrock documentation, and incorrect defaults; the ADR and framework doc must be kept in line with code."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785812210246199605,"uuid":"397ce8d5-e2a0-4a9c-b116-7bb70f09a2ea"}